437: /// Read a symlink entry's target string with a hard size cap so a deflate
438: /// bomb posing as a symlink can't balloon the heap.
439: /// Case-fold + NFC-normalise a path for use as a `link_map` key. This is what
440: /// APFS and NTFS do at lookup time, so two names that the kernel would treat as
441: /// the same inode produce the same key here. On case-sensitive volumes this is
442: /// conservative (may follow a hop the FS wouldn't), which only ever causes an
443: /// extra rejection — never an extra acceptance.
444: fn fold_key(p: &Path) -> String {
445:     p.to_string_lossy()
446:         .nfc()
447:         .flat_map(char::to_lowercase)
